{'query': 'public transportation cost in Singapore for tourists', 'results': [{'title': 'How much it costs to travel around Singapore (bus, taxi, and more)', 'url': 'https://reachingsingapore.com/transport-costs-singapore', 'snippet': 'The Singapore Tourist Pass is technically an EZ Link card loaded with 1, 2, or 3 days of unlimited rides that starts at S$22. I generally do not recommend buying the Singapore Tourist Pass for the unlimited rides as you to use a lot of public transport to make it worth it.'}, {'title': 'How to Use Public Transportation in Singapore for Tourists', 'url': 'https://www.thesingaporeblog.com/public-transportation-in-singapore-for-tourists/', 'snippet': 'Learn how tourists use public transportation in Singapore. MRT, buses, costs, passes, and how to pay explained clearly.'}, {'title': 'Public transport fares & passes | Public Transport Council', 'url': 'https://www.ptc.gov.sg/fares/public-transport-fares-and-passes/', 'snippet': 'Public transport fares & passes PTC fare structure: distance-based bus & train fares, cash vs card rates, and concessions for students, seniors & more.'}, {'title': 'Fares | Public Transport Council', 'url': 'https://www.ptc.gov.sg/fares/', 'snippet': 'Find out more about current bus and train fares, concession fares, and monthly passes for your travel needs.'}, {'title': 'Getting around Singapore: the tourist transport guide (2026 fares ...', 'url': 'https://singaporecity360.com/the-best-way-to-get-around-singapore-public-transportation-guide-for-tourists/', 'snippet': 'Transfers to or from non-public buses - premium, shuttle, temporary, special, privately operated cross-border and tourist buses - do not qualify as valid transfers. A private shuttle fare is paid on top of the public fare AND ends the fare journey, so a following public leg starts a fresh journey at the first band.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 2.31666829995811}
